paragraphs.text:
Section 19(1)
of the Contempt of Courts Act is as follows :
An appeal shall lie as of right from any order or decision of High Court in exercise of its jurisdiction to punish for contempt-
(a) where the order or decision is that of a single Judge, to a Bench of not less than two Judges of the Court;
(b) where the order or decision is that of a Bench, to the Supreme Court;
Provided that where the order or decision is that of the Court of the Judicial Commissioner in any Union Territory, such appeal shall lie to the Supreme Court.

